# FIX-2026-09-22 (audit item 3): promote backups + atomic-write temp files are
# runtime byproducts of scripts/update_ics.py and must never be committed.
# The canonical table keeps a .bak/.bak.N rotation (newest = .bak); the atomic
# writer stages bytes in a sibling .tmp before os.replace.
*.bak
*.bak.[0-9]*
*.json.tmp
# Node (no package.json manifest — deps are not reproducible; the JS
# tests in tests_frontend.js are dependency-free Node scripts)
node_modules/
# OS
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
_huge.bin
# E2E literature-figure test data (UI-REVIEW-2026-09-07): copyrighted
# paper figures + per-run API test results stay local, never on GitHub.
outputs/e2e_radiolaria/
outputs/e2e_oa/
# Same class of data, larger (AUDIT-2026-09-28): the lit2020 corpora are 522
# cropped figures out of 2020 stratigraphy papers -- 299.66 MB across the three
# directories. They are INPUT to tests_real_corpus.py, not fixtures; the
# committed half of that work is tests/fixtures/real_payloads/ (8 model
# responses, 113 KB) plus the invariant checks in tests/test_generic_tables.py,
# so the corpus itself stays local for the same licensing reason as above.
outputs/lit2020/
outputs/lit2020_all/
outputs/lit2020_sample/
# Per-run report written by tests_real_corpus.py (its --report default). It
# embeds captions and table counts from those copyrighted figures.
outputs/real_corpus_report.json
# Local API credentials for the e2e harness (defense in depth — the file
# itself lives outside the repo in %TEMP%).
rca_e2e_api.env
# FE-FIX-2026-09-22 (server cleanup finding 3): PID-suffixed scratch files
# the server test suites write into assets/ to exercise ETag/streaming.
# Both tests delete them (try/finally + a module teardown sweep), this glob
# is defense in depth so a hard-killed run can never dirty the tree.
assets/_fe_p_perf_*.css
assets/_fe_f_*.css
